Rust-native compiler front-end pipeline

The compiler front-end used to lower the surface AST into eqlog-eqlog
nodes and let downstream passes consume them as eqlog facts. This
branch replaces that path with plain Rust passes operating on a flat
id-based arena, retiring the eqlog-eqlog grammar bridge for the
front-end.

New passes (each in its own module under eqlog/src/):

  - ast.rs: id-based arena AST built directly by the lalrpop grammar.
  - scopes.rs: scope resolution to symbols, with per-decl entries.
  - casing.rs, scope_checks/, syntactic.rs: casing, occurrence,
    binding and structural checks emitting CompileErrors.
  - algebra/signature.rs: dependent signature (types, preds, funcs)
    derived from the AST.
  - algebra/populate.rs: walks rule bodies into per-rule
    RuleStructures, mapping AST terms to Els and recording statement
    before/after structures.
  - algebra/structure.rs: per-rule Structures with element
    unification, FuncApp/PredApp tables, and a Structure::close pass
    that saturates under functionality and signature-imposed typing.
    StructureCat layers a forward-only family of morphisms on top and
    propagates shared data between structures.
  - algebra/mod.rs: drives populate and close to a joint fixed point
    and lowers per-rule TypeConflicts into user-facing CompileErrors.

TypeConflict carries both ConcreteTypes (TypeId plus parent ElId
list). When two ConcreteTypes get assigned to the same equivalence
class with the same TypeId but parents in distinct classes, the close
pass records a parent disagreement instead of silently unifying the
parents — the previous behaviour collapsed distinct ambient parents,
which is wrong in the multi-model setting. Parent disagreements are
deferred during the close fixed point and re-evaluated under the
final unification, so observation order on pending_equalities does
not matter. A new CompileError::ConflictingParentEl variant reports
the locations of the two terms backing the innermost differing
parent.

The legacy eqlog-eqlog semantics module and ast_to_eqlog helper
remain for the parts that still need them, but front-end checks no
longer route through eqlog facts.
